+# Narrowing NG-9 for the Veterinarian Specialty Filter
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declared searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian out of scope, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The veterinarian directory already presents each veterinarian's specialties. A request has arrived to let a reader narrow that directory to the veterinarians holding a named specialty, on both the page and the machine-readable surface.
+
+This surfaces a boundary question NG-9 did not settle: does the decline cover any veterinarian lookup, or only free-text search over veterinarian records?
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 as written** — treat any veterinarian lookup, an attribute filter included, as declined.
+2. **Narrow NG-9** — keep free-text veterinarian search out of scope, but admit filtering the directory by an attribute it already displays.
+
+## Decision
+
+Narrow NG-9. Free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope. Filtering the directory by a specialty it already shows is in scope, realized by REQ-VET-004 across both directory surfaces. NG-9 now declines only free-text search of pets, visits, and veterinarians.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The veterinarian directory gains a specialty filter without opening a general search surface.
+- The boundary to maintain: matching a whole attribute value the directory already displays is in scope; free-text search over veterinarian records is not.
+- Owner search remains the only free-text search in the system, preserving what NG-9 set out to teach once.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+## References
+
+- [PRD: Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-004)
