+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also published in a machine-readable form at a second address; this is a supported surface, carrying the same veterinarians and specialties as the page `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Both directory surfaces accept an optional specialty filter, expressed only through the request URL — no page control accompanies it in this capability. Matching is on the whole specialty name and ignores letter case; it is not a prefix match, so a partial value matches nothing. A specialty no veterinarian holds yields the directory with an empty veterinarian list and a normal, successful response rather than an error. An empty or whitespace-only filter value behaves as if no filter were given, the same way an empty owner search returns every owner. Without a filter, both surfaces behave as they did before. On the paged surface the filter is preserved across page navigation, so a filtered directory stays navigable `[REQ-VET-004]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable directory is requested, then it returns the same veterinarians and their specialties as the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a filter naming a held specialty, differing from it only by letter case, when either surface is requested, then only veterinarians holding that specialty are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a filter that only partially matches a specialty name, when either surface is requested, then no veterinarian matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a filter naming a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is requested, then the directory is returned with an empty veterinarian list and a successful response.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given an empty or whitespace-only filter value, when either surface is requested, then the result matches a request with no filter.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given no filter, when either surface is requested, then every veterinarian is listed as before.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a filtered paged directory, when a page-navigation link is followed, then the same filter still applies on the next page.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
